# Redux Toolkit State Management

## Store Setup

```ts
// store/store.ts
import { configureStore } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";
import { baseApi } from "./api/baseApi";
import { authSlice } from "./slices/authSlice";
import { uiSlice } from "./slices/uiSlice";

export const store = configureStore({
  reducer: {
    [baseApi.reducerPath]: baseApi.reducer,
    auth: authSlice.reducer,
    ui: uiSlice.reducer,
  },
  middleware: (getDefault) => getDefault().concat(baseApi.middleware),
});

export type RootState = ReturnType<typeof store.getState>;
export type AppDispatch = typeof store.dispatch;
```

## Typed Hooks

```ts
// store/hooks.ts
import { useDispatch, useSelector, type TypedUseSelectorHook } from "react-redux";
import type { RootState, AppDispatch } from "./store";

export const useAppDispatch = useDispatch.withTypes<AppDispatch>();
export const useAppSelector: TypedUseSelectorHook<RootState> = useSelector;
```

## When to Use What

| Data Type | Where to Store | Example |
|-----------|---------------|---------|
| Server data (clients, assignments) | RTK Query cache | `useGetClientsQuery()` |
| Auth state (current user, role) | Redux slice | `authSlice` |
| UI state (sidebar open, filters) | Redux slice | `uiSlice` |
| Form input state | Local `useState` | Form fields before submit |
| Ephemeral UI (tooltips, hovers) | Local `useState` | Component-level only |

## Slice Conventions

```ts
// store/slices/uiSlice.ts
import { createSlice, type PayloadAction } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";

interface UiState {
  sidebarOpen: boolean;
  activeOfficeFilter: string | null;
}

const initialState: UiState = {
  sidebarOpen: true,
  activeOfficeFilter: null,
};

export const uiSlice = createSlice({
  name: "ui",
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    toggleSidebar(state) {
      state.sidebarOpen = !state.sidebarOpen;
    },
    setOfficeFilter(state, action: PayloadAction<string | null>) {
      state.activeOfficeFilter = action.payload;
    },
  },
});

export const { toggleSidebar, setOfficeFilter } = uiSlice.actions;
```

## Rules

- Always use `useAppSelector` and `useAppDispatch` (typed), never plain `useSelector`/`useDispatch`
- Server data lives in RTK Query cache — don't duplicate into slices
- Slices only for client-side state (auth, UI preferences, filters)
- Never mutate state outside Immer (RTK's `createSlice` handles this)
- Selectors in the same file as the slice, exported as named functions
- Keep slices small and focused — one per concern
